   "The object reads well at a glance as a hive frame. It has a wooden top bar with ear-lugs, side bars, a bottom bar, gold hex comb and a honey drip, and its colours fit the house look.",
   "The 'glow' doesn't read as glow. The halo ellipse behind the frame (rx 66, ry 46, fill 'light', a 0.12) shows up as a flat dull-grey disc on the charcoal background, like a shadow or a stain. The line says 'glowing like a captured sunset', but nothing warm comes off the comb.",
   "In the held-in-both-hands view, neither hand grips the ear-lugs. The frame floats over the chest with no visible hands at its ends, and the arms flare out sideways behind it like wings. The spec says it is lifted by its long ear-lugs, so the hands must sit at the lug tips.",
   "The pale capped-cell patches are scattered in random blobs, so they read as damage or mould rather than 'full of capped honeycomb'. Capped honey should be the main surface, with only a few open amber cells.",
   "The drip under the bottom bar hangs off-centre (right of middle) and barely touches the bar, so it reads as a loose floating shape at small scale."
